title: Leftcom Newspaper Founded
new-page: true
view-if: german_negotiations >= 8 or (german_negotiations >= 4 and month = 2 and week >= 3) or (german_negotiations >= 4 and party_congress_timer <= 1)
max-visits: 1
tags: event
on-arrival: {!
  Q.b_dissent += 0.1; 
  Q.leftcom_strength += 10; 
  Q.leninist_unrest += 5; 
!}

= Founding of Kommunist

The <span style="color: var(--leftcom); font-weight: bold;">Leftcoms</span> have announced the creation of their own newspaper, <i>Kommunist</i>, with articles promoting "revolutionary war" and decrying capitulation to the Germans. Though a relatively small organ so far, it appears the faction seeks to use it to win over delegates to the upcoming party congress.   

- @condemn
- @nothing

@condemn
title: Condemn the paper and seek to censure its editors in the Petrograd Soviet fraction. 
on-arrival: {!
  if ((Q.leninist_strength + Q.moderate_strength) > Q.leftcom_strength) { Q.leftcom_strength -= 5; Q.leftcom_dissent += 10; }
!}

[?if ((leninist_strength + moderate_strength) > leftcom_strength) : A resolution is passed in the party fraction of the Petrograd Soviet censuring the editors for impropriety. The <span style="color: var(--leftcom); font-weight: bold;">Leftcoms</span> complain that we they are being unfairly restricted. ?]
[?if ((leninist_strength + moderate_strength) <= leftcom_strength) : Though the newspaper is criticized by the <span style="color: var(--bolshevik-color); font-weight: bold;">Leninists</span>, it appears the <span style="color: var(--leftcom); font-weight: bold;">Leftcoms</span> have sufficient strength to block any kind of formal sanction, allowing the newspaper to continue unimpeded. ?]

@nothing
title: There's nothing we can do.
go-to: root 
